# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Lejia Zeng et al. (2026). Developing a Machine-Learning Interatomic Potential for Non-Covalent Interactions in Proteins.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:  arXiv:2601.11628v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2601.11628v2 (sha256 edd27b7c31f80127...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 514 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zeng2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the PANIP ensemble (5 NequIP models) trained directly
# on counterpoise-corrected wB97X-D3BJ/def2-TZVPP interaction energies
# of about 3.15 million PDB fragment dimers selected by multi-fidelity
# active learning (r2SCAN-3c surrogate labels), its interaction-energy
# errors on four benchmark sets, and ANI-2x on the CSD set. Errors are
# interaction-energy errors (kcal/mol). Binding-pose and PDB pattern
# analyses are not metrics.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-zeng2026 a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Zeng et al. (2026): PANIP, a NequIP ensemble for protein non-covalent interaction energies trained on the multi-fidelity active-learning PDB-FRAGID dataset" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-zeng2026 .

entity:article-zeng2026 a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
