# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Evaluating 15,300 random dimers on one CPU core took PANIP 6 h 11 min versus an estimated 463 days 11 h for wB97X-D3BJ/def2-TZVPP (Results).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The low-energy benchmark is described as the training domain without saying whether it was held out, so its role is null. The PDB-FRAGID size is approximate (about 3.15 million); no n. No DOI in the manifest; authors taken from the paper's front matter.
